; host/record.bl — the pinned HOST MODULE for `Elixir.BeamLisp.Record`.
;
; `BeamLisp.Record` is beam-lisp's `defrecord`/`deftype` type factory: it
; creates the struct module a `defrecord` names, keeps the module→fields
; registry the runtime reads (`BeamLisp.Ns.Rt`, `core`, the reader), and builds
; instances (a struct for a record, a `{:bl_deftype, mod, fields}` tagged tuple
; for a deftype). This file is the `.bl` port of `lib/beam_lisp/record.ex`,
; compiled by `BeamLisp.AOT/compile_host_file` into ONE exact-named beam whose
; top-level `defn`s are plain exported functions — the exact call surface every
; caller already names at `Elixir.BeamLisp.Record`, so no caller is renamed.
;
; This file owns SOURCE and TESTS only. The seed entry that points it at
; `Elixir.BeamLisp.Record` — and the `@pinned_host_sources` row that keeps the
; codegen key following `record.bl` instead of the deleted `record.ex` — are
; written by the wave that deletes `record.ex`, the family convention every
; pinned port in `priv/host/` follows. Nothing in `aot_cache.ex`, `seed.bl` or
; `record.ex` is touched here.
;
; ABI PARITY IS THE CONTRACT. Every function below reproduces its Elixir
; counterpart clause for clause — the same standard-library primitives, the
; same evaluation order, the same return types, the same exception class and
; message — so the pinned beam stands in for the module every caller already
; names, and the port is a no-op at every call site. The shapes that are easy
; to get subtly wrong and are therefore deliberate:
;
;   * THE MODULE THIS SOURCE BECAME IS READ, NEVER NAMED. `self-mod/0` reads
;     the atom from a fun literal compiled into this file
;     (`erlang/fun_info(F, :module)` — the `priv/host/decimal.bl` /
;     `vector.bl` idiom), and three things follow from it:
;       - `module_name/2` composes `Module.concat([self_mod, …])`, so a
;         `defrecord` at the production atom builds
;         `BeamLisp.Record.<Ns>.<Name>` EXACTLY as the live module did, while
;         the same bytes compiled at a probe atom build that probe's records.
;       - the registry key is `{self_mod, :registry}`, exactly the live
;         `{__MODULE__, :registry}` at production and an isolated table under
;         a probe.
;       - the `__struct__` clauses `create_module/3` emits call
;         `self_mod.generated_struct(…)`, so the struct a beam builds points
;         back at the beam that built it.
;     No `BeamLisp.Record` literal appears anywhere in this file.
;
;   * `is_bl_map/1`, INLINED. The live `map_construct/2` head is guarded by
;     `BeamLisp.Guards.is_bl_map/1`, a `defguard` — a COMPILE-TIME macro that
;     expands to `is_map(x) and not is_struct(x)`. A pinned file has no
;     `defguard`/`import` of another module's macros, and the guard vocabulary
;     has no `is_struct`, so the predicate is written here as `bl-map?/1` (a
;     plain function, the `priv/host/transient.bl` `bl-map?` shape) and the
;     clause is a body-level `if`. Without the exclusion the clause would
;     swallow every struct — the exact bug the guard exists to name.
;
;   * A FAILED GUARD IS A REAL `FunctionClauseError`. `map_construct/2`,
;     `construct_list/2` and `build_type/2` raise the
;     `FunctionClauseError` their live clause heads raised, built by
;     `clause-error/2` with THIS beam's own module atom — so a probe compile
;     names the probe atom, exactly as the pinned family does.
;
;   * `:__struct__`/`:__info__` ARE DESCRIPTOR DATA, NOT defns. `create_module/3`
;     and `struct_info_clauses/2` build `BeamLisp.Emit` clause maps and lower
;     them through `Emit.descriptor_for/2` + `Emit.compile_descriptor/1`, then
;     `:code.purge`/`:code.delete`/`Emit.load_binary!/2` — the SAME two-phase
;     "compile the whole replacement before touching the loaded module" order
;     the live module used. No quoted route, no `Module.create`.
;
;   * `[__struct__: 0, __struct__: 1]` and `%{__struct__: mod}` in the live
;     source are an Erlang LIST of 2-tuples and an Erlang MAP. Here they are
;     written `(list (tuple …) …)` and `{:__struct__ mod}`; a `[…]` literal
;     would be a `BeamLisp.Vector` and would change the emitted term.
;
;   * `Enum.reduce(fields, MapSet.new(), fn field, seen -> … end)` returns a
;     MapSet in the live module but `validate_struct_fields!/1` discards it and
;     answers `:ok`; the same shape is kept and the `:ok` is what is returned.
;
; ONE DELIBERATE BEHAVIOURAL EDGE. The live `generated_struct/3`
; destructures each kv element with `fn {key, value}, struct ->`, so a
; NON-2-tuple pair fails the anonymous clause. That failure names the anonymous
; fn with a COMPILER-GENERATED atom (`…-generated_struct/3-inlined-0-`), an
; inlining detail of whichever compiler built `record.ex` rather than an ABI.
; This port makes the SAME refusal — the same class, the same `data`, a pair of
; any other shape is rejected — and raises the plain anonymous
; `FunctionClauseError` ("no function clause matches") rather than reproduce an
; artefact name that would drift with the compiler.
;
; THE EXPORT SURFACE IS THE LIVE ONE PLUS THIS FILE'S HELPERS. A pinned module
; exports exactly its file's defns, so the helpers `record.ex` keeps private
; (`self-mod`, `struct-like?`, `bl-map?`, `clause-error`, `registry-key`,
; `module_name`, `validate_struct_fields!`, `struct_info_clauses`,
; `create_module`, `register`) are exports on this beam. That is the ONE
; deliberate divergence, the same one every pinned port in `priv/host/` carries.
;
; DEPENDENCY SHAPE. The whole file is written against `:erlang` BIFs
; (`is_map`, `is_map_key`, `map_get`, `is_atom`, `is_tuple`, `tuple_size`,
; `element`, `is_list`, `length`, `fun_info`, `term_to_binary`, `self`),
; `:code`/`:global`/`:persistent_term`/`:crypto`, the Elixir standard library
; (`Elixir.Enum`, `Elixir.Map`, `Elixir.MapSet`, `Elixir.List`, `Elixir.String`,
; `Elixir.Macro`, `Elixir.Module`, `Elixir.IO`, `Elixir.Kernel`) and the
; pinned `BeamLisp.Emit`. `literal/3` calls `BeamLisp.Env.fetch/2`, the SAME
; entry the live module calls, and only at RUNTIME (a `#Name{…}` literal the
; reader reads, long after boot); `create_module/3` reaches
; `BeamLisp.Ns.Anf`/`BeamLisp.Ns.Lower` through `Emit` only when a
; `defrecord`/`deftype` form is EVALUATED, which is exactly when the live
; module reached them. No beam-lisp namespace is named directly.
;
; Run: bin/bl test test/bl/host_record_test.bl

(ns host.record)

; ── module-exact self reference ───────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- self-mod
  "The atom THIS source was compiled into, read from a fun literal compiled
   into this file — module-exact, so the same source serves the production
   atom in the seed and a probe atom under test without naming either."
  []
  (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module)))

; ── predicates (the runtime face of the live guard macros) ───────────────

(defn- struct-like?
  "Elixir's `is_struct/1`: a map carrying an atom `:__struct__` tag. A binary
   tag is NOT a struct, and neither is a bare map."
  [x]
  (and (erlang/is_map x)
       (erlang/is_map_key :__struct__ x)
       (erlang/is_atom (erlang/map_get :__struct__ x))))

(defn- bl-map?
  "The live `is_bl_map/1`: a plain map — a map that is NOT a struct."
  [x]
  (and (erlang/is_map x) (erlang/not (struct-like? x))))

; ── errors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- clause-error
  "The `FunctionClauseError` an unmatched clause head raised, named with the
   FUNCTION and ARITY of the clause that failed — so a refusal reads exactly
   as the live module's did."
  [fname arity]
  (erlang/error
    (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
      (list (tuple :module (self-mod))
            (tuple :function fname)
            (tuple :arity arity)))))

(defn- argument-error
  "`ArgumentError.exception/1` from a message binary, raised."
  [message]
  (erlang/error (Elixir.ArgumentError/exception message)))

; ── the registry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- registry-key
  "The `:persistent_term` key the module→`{kind, ns, name, fields}` table lives
   under — the live `{__MODULE__, :registry}`."
  []
  (tuple (self-mod) :registry))

(defn- register
  "Record a freshly created module's `{kind, ns, name, fields}` entry."
  [mod kind ns name fields]
  ;; Different class origins may publish concurrently. Their per-module
  ;; locks do not serialize this shared persistent-term map's read/modify/write.
  ;; Hold this distinct registry fence only for the native map update; never
  ;; acquire a module lock or run user code while it is held.
  (BeamLisp.Env/with_generation_lock (tuple :record-registry (self-mod))
    (fn []
      (persistent_term/put
        (registry-key)
        (Map/put (persistent_term/get (registry-key) {}) mod (tuple kind ns name fields))))))

; ── type predicates ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn record?
  "True for a record instance (a registered record struct)."
  [v]
  (if (struct-like? v)
    (record_module? (erlang/map_get :__struct__ v))
    false))

(defn record_module?
  "True for a record's module atom."
  [mod]
  (if (erlang/is_atom mod)
    (let [i (info mod)]
      (and (erlang/is_tuple i)
           (erlang/== 4 (erlang/tuple_size i))
           (erlang/== :record (erlang/element 1 i))))
    false))

(defn deftype_module?
  "True for a deftype's module atom."
  [mod]
  (if (erlang/is_atom mod)
    (let [i (info mod)]
      (and (erlang/is_tuple i)
           (erlang/== 4 (erlang/tuple_size i))
           (erlang/== :deftype (erlang/element 1 i))))
    false))

(defn info
  "The registry entry `{kind, ns, name, fields}` for `mod`, or nil."
  [mod]
  (if (erlang/is_atom mod)
    (let [reg (persistent_term/get (registry-key) {})]
      (if (erlang/is_map_key mod reg) (erlang/map_get mod reg) nil))
    nil))

(defn fields_of
  "The declared field names (atoms, in definition order) of a record/deftype."
  [mod]
  (let [i (info mod)]
    (if (erlang/== nil i)
      (argument-error (str "not a beam-lisp record/deftype: " (Kernel/inspect mod)))
      (erlang/element 4 i))))

; ── definition ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn define
  "Define a canonical record through one atomic native publication boundary."
  [ns name fields]
  (publish_declaration! (declaration_descriptor ns name :record fields)))

(defn define_type
  "Define a canonical deftype through one atomic native publication boundary."
  [ns name fields]
  (publish_declaration! (declaration_descriptor ns name :deftype fields)))

; ── construction ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn positional_ctor
  "The positional constructor `->Name`: a variadic (min-0) fn so the handler
   receives the whole argument list at once. Arity is checked against the field
   count; a record builds a struct, a deftype a tagged tuple."
  [mod]
  (let [i (info mod)]
    (if (erlang/== nil i)
      (argument-error (str "not a beam-lisp record/deftype: " (Kernel/inspect mod)))
      (let [kind (erlang/element 1 i)
            name (erlang/element 3 i)
            fields (erlang/element 4 i)
            n (erlang/length fields)]
        (tuple :"$blfn" {}
          (tuple 0
            (fn [args]
              (if (erlang/== (erlang/length args) n)
                (if (erlang/== kind :record)
                  (struct_map mod (Enum/zip fields args))
                  (tuple :bl_deftype mod (List/to_tuple args)))
                (argument-error
                  (str "wrong number of args (" (erlang/length args) ") for "
                       name " constructor, expected " n))))))))))

(defn map_ctor
  "The `map->Name` constructor: a record built from a map's known fields."
  [mod]
  (fn [m] (map_construct mod m)))

(defn struct_map
  "Build a record struct from `{field, value}` pairs (fields not given default
   to nil)."
  [mod kv]
  (Map/put (Map/new kv) :__struct__ mod))

(defn map_construct
  "Build a record from a map, taking only its declared fields. A record is
   built from a *plain* map's declared fields — a struct source would leak its
   internal `__struct__` into the new record."
  [mod m]
  (if (bl-map? m)
    (let [fields (fields_of mod)]
      (Map/put
        (Map/merge (Map/new fields (fn [f] (tuple f nil))) (Map/take m fields))
        :__struct__ mod))
    (clause-error :map_construct 2)))

(defn construct_list
  "Build a record from a positional argument list (used by `construct_list`
   callers and the `->Name` body)."
  [mod values]
  (if (erlang/is_list values)
    (let [fields (fields_of mod)]
      (if (erlang/== (erlang/length values) (erlang/length fields))
        (struct_map mod (Enum/zip fields values))
        (argument-error
          (str "wrong number of values (" (erlang/length values) ") for record "
               (Kernel/inspect mod) ", expected " (erlang/length fields)))))
    (clause-error :construct_list 2)))

(defn literal
  "Resolve a `#Name{...}` (or `#ns/Name{...}`) record literal read by the
   reader against `ns` and construct the record from the given map."
  [ns name fields_map]
  (let [r (BeamLisp.Env/fetch ns name)]
    (if (and (erlang/is_tuple r)
             (erlang/== 2 (erlang/tuple_size r))
             (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r))
             (erlang/is_atom (erlang/element 2 r)))
      (let [mod (erlang/element 2 r)]
        (if (record_module? mod)
          (map_construct mod fields_map)
          (erlang/error
            (Elixir.RuntimeError/exception
              (str "record literal " name " does not name a record")))))
      (erlang/error
        (Elixir.RuntimeError/exception
          (str "record literal " name ": no such record in namespace " ns))))))

; ── deftype field access ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn build_type
  "Build a deftype instance from its positional field values."
  [mod values]
  (if (erlang/is_list values)
    (tuple :bl_deftype mod (List/to_tuple values))
    (clause-error :build_type 2)))

(defn deftype_field
  "Read a deftype field by name: `(.-x obj)` and `(.x obj)`. Records do not
   support field access (they use keyword lookup); only a deftype tuple reaches
   here — a `{:bl_reify, …}` or any other value is the live `ArgumentError`."
  [obj field]
  (if (and (erlang/is_tuple obj)
           (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size obj))
           (erlang/== :bl_deftype (erlang/element 1 obj)))
    (let [mod (erlang/element 2 obj)
          tup (erlang/element 3 obj)
          fields (fields_of mod)
          i (Enum/find_index fields (fn [f] (erlang/== f field)))]
      (if (erlang/== nil i)
        (argument-error (str "no field " (Kernel/inspect field) " on " (Kernel/inspect mod)))
        (erlang/element (erlang/+ i 1) tup)))
    (argument-error (str "field access on a non-deftype: " (Kernel/inspect obj)))))

; ── internals ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- module_name
  "`defrecord`/`deftype` run in a namespace; the struct module is scoped by it
   so two namespaces may each define their own `Point` without colliding.
   Namespace dots nest, so `geometry` → `<self>.Geometry.Point`."
  [ns name]
  (let [segments (Enum/map (String/split ns ".") (fn [s] (Macro/camelize s)))]
    (Module/concat (erlang/++ (list (self-mod)) (erlang/++ segments (list name))))))

(defn generated_struct
  "The zeroed struct for `mod` (arity 2) or a `kv`-filled one (arity 3), the
   functions the emitted `__struct__/0,1` clauses call. A key outside the
   declared `fields` is the live `KeyError`."
  ([mod fields]
   (Map/put (Map/new fields (fn [f] (tuple f nil))) :__struct__ mod))
  ([mod fields kv]
   (Enum/reduce kv (generated_struct mod fields)
     (fn [pair struct]
       ; the live `fn {key, value}, struct ->` accepts a 2-TUPLE and nothing
       ; else, and its clause failure is a compiler-generated ANONYMOUS fn —
       ; its `module`/`function`/`arity` name an inlining artefact of the
       ; compiler that built `record.ex` (`…-generated_struct/3-inlined-0-`),
       ; not an ABI. The SAME rejection, class and `data` are kept here; only
       ; that unnameable artefact is dropped, so the message reads the plain
       ; anonymous "no function clause matches". See the header.
       (if (and (erlang/is_tuple pair) (erlang/== 2 (erlang/tuple_size pair)))
         (let [key (erlang/element 1 pair)
               value (erlang/element 2 pair)]
           (if (Enum/member? fields key)
             (Map/put struct key value)
             (erlang/error (Elixir.KeyError/exception (list (tuple :key key) (tuple :term struct))))))
         (erlang/error (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception (list))))))))

(defn- class_descriptor
  "Compile the complete replacement before touching the loaded module or
   registry."
  [mod kind fields]
  (let [clauses
        (if (erlang/== kind :record)
          (erlang/++
            (list
              (BeamLisp.Emit/function_clause :__struct__
                (BeamLisp.Emit/remote (self-mod) :generated_struct
                  (list (BeamLisp.Emit/lit mod) (BeamLisp.Emit/lit fields))))
              (BeamLisp.Emit/function_clause :__struct__
                (BeamLisp.Emit/remote (self-mod) :generated_struct
                  (list (BeamLisp.Emit/lit mod) (BeamLisp.Emit/lit fields) (BeamLisp.Emit/var "kv")))
                (list {:pop :pvar :name "kv"})))
            (struct_info_clauses mod fields))
          (list (BeamLisp.Emit/function_clause :__bl_deftype__ (BeamLisp.Emit/lit true))))
        descriptor (BeamLisp.Emit/descriptor_for mod clauses)] descriptor))

(defn declaration_descriptor
  "Pure compiler producer for a named record/deftype. Never loads code, interns
   a constructor, changes a registry or starts an initializer. Field order is
   part of the immutable type identity; actor authority is never granted."
  [ns name kind fields]
  (when-not (and (erlang/is_binary ns) (erlang/> (erlang/byte_size ns) 0)
                (erlang/=< (erlang/byte_size ns) 512)
                (erlang/is_binary name) (erlang/> (erlang/byte_size name) 0)
                (erlang/=< (erlang/byte_size name) 128)
                (Enum/member? (list :record :deftype) kind)
                (erlang/is_list fields) (erlang/=< (erlang/length fields) 256)
                (Enum/all? fields (fn [field]
                  (and (erlang/is_binary field) (erlang/> (erlang/byte_size field) 0)
                       (erlang/=< (erlang/byte_size field) 128)))))
    (argument-error "invalid immutable record/deftype declaration"))
  (let [mod (module_name ns name)
        field-atoms (Enum/map fields (fn [field] (String/to_atom field)))
        _ (when (and (erlang/== :record kind) (Enum/member? field-atoms :__struct__))
            (argument-error "cannot set :__struct__ in struct definition"))
        descriptor (class_descriptor mod kind (if (erlang/== :record kind) field-atoms (list)))
        existing (info mod) wanted (tuple kind ns name field-atoms)]
    (when (and existing
               (erlang/not (erlang/== (tuple (elem existing 0) (elem existing 1) (elem existing 2))
                                     (tuple kind ns name))))
      (argument-error "record/deftype module already belongs to a different declaration origin"))
    (Map/put descriptor :attrs
      (list (BeamLisp.Vector/new (list :bl_generated_class
                  (tuple 1 ns name kind fields)))))))

(defn declaration_kind
  "Recognize only this producer's canonical class body at an actual compiler
   declaration site. Unit stamps may be added later; they confer no actor role."
  [descriptor ns name]
  (let [attributes (Map/get descriptor :attrs (list))
        metadata (Enum/find_value attributes
                    (fn [entry]
                      (let [parts (if (erlang/is_tuple entry) (Tuple/to_list entry)
                                      (if (erlang/is_list entry) entry
                                        (BeamLisp.Vector/to_list entry)))]
                        (when (and (erlang/== 2 (erlang/length parts))
                                   (erlang/== :bl_generated_class (erlang/hd parts)))
                          (erlang/hd (erlang/tl parts))))))]
    (when (and (erlang/is_tuple metadata) (erlang/== 5 (erlang/tuple_size metadata))
               (erlang/== 1 (elem metadata 0)) (erlang/== ns (elem metadata 1))
               (erlang/== name (elem metadata 2)))
      (let [kind (elem metadata 3)
            canonical (declaration_descriptor ns name kind (elem metadata 4))]
        (let [unit-keys (list :bl_source_hash :bl_compiler_key :bl_unit_source_digest
                             :bl_aot_artifact_version :bl_unit_namespace
                             :bl_declaration_owner :bl_generated_class_version
                             :bl_aot_artifact_role)
              clean (Enum/reject attributes
                      (fn [entry]
                        (let [parts (if (erlang/is_tuple entry) (Tuple/to_list entry)
                                        (if (erlang/is_list entry) entry
                                          (BeamLisp.Vector/to_list entry)))]
                          (and (erlang/== 2 (erlang/length parts))
                               (Enum/member? unit-keys (erlang/hd parts))))))]
          (when (and (erlang/== clean (Map/get canonical :attrs))
                     (erlang/== (Map/drop descriptor (list :attrs :ann))
                                (Map/drop canonical (list :attrs :ann)))) kind))))))

(defn declaration_metadata [descriptor]
  (Enum/find_value (Map/get descriptor :attrs (list))
    (fn [entry]
      (let [parts (if (erlang/is_tuple entry) (Tuple/to_list entry)
                      (if (erlang/is_list entry) entry (BeamLisp.Vector/to_list entry)))]
        (when (and (erlang/== 2 (erlang/length parts))
                   (erlang/== :bl_generated_class (erlang/hd parts)))
          (erlang/hd (erlang/tl parts)))))))
(defn- class_identity! [descriptor]
  (let [metadata (declaration_metadata descriptor)]
    (when-not (and (erlang/is_tuple metadata) (erlang/== 5 (erlang/tuple_size metadata))
                   (declaration_kind descriptor (elem metadata 1) (elem metadata 2)))
      (argument-error "not a canonical record/deftype descriptor"))
    metadata))
(defn- loaded_md5? [mod expected]
  (and (erlang/module_loaded mod)
       (erlang/== expected (erlang/apply mod :module_info (list :md5)))))
; Consistency check ONLY. Loaded attributes do not grant SDK/actor authority.
(defn- loaded_class_identity? [mod metadata]
  (and (erlang/module_loaded mod)
       (let [actual (erlang/apply :proplists :get_value
                      (list :bl_generated_class (erlang/apply mod :module_info (list :attributes))))]
         ;; Native descriptor artifacts expose direct values; ordinary OTP
         ;; attribute collection may wrap one value. Both must match exactly.
         (or (erlang/== metadata actual) (erlang/== (list metadata) actual)))))

(defn- publish_class! [descriptor pair expected]
  (let [metadata (class_identity! descriptor) ns (elem metadata 1) name (elem metadata 2)
        kind (elem metadata 3) fields (elem metadata 4) mod (Map/fetch! descriptor :name)]
    (when-not (and (erlang/is_binary expected) (erlang/== 16 (erlang/byte_size expected)))
      (argument-error "invalid compiler-emitted class digest"))
    (global/trans (tuple mod (erlang/self))
      (fn []
        ;; Origin registry and physical class code share one atomic native
        ;; module fence. Unleased ordinary dev edits remain supported; a live
        ;; class can never change either its executable bytes OR field schema.
        (BeamLisp.Env/with_module_locks (list mod)
         (fn []
          (declaration_descriptor ns name kind fields)
          (let [existing (info mod)
                wanted (tuple kind ns name (Enum/map fields (fn [field] (String/to_atom field))))
                changed (or (erlang/not (loaded_md5? mod expected))
                            (and existing (erlang/not (erlang/== existing wanted))))]
           ;; The first retained deftype has no registry row yet and its
           ;; executable MD5 omits fields. Require the exact compiler-produced
           ;; schema on the loaded artifact before accepting that registration.
           ;; This consistency check never confers SDK or actor authority.
           (when (and (erlang/== nil existing) (BeamLisp.Env/live_code_leases? mod)
                      (erlang/not (loaded_class_identity? mod metadata)))
            (erlang/error (tuple :leased_class_identity_unregistered mod)))
           (when (and changed (BeamLisp.Env/live_code_leases? mod))
            (erlang/error (tuple :code_leased mod)))
           (when (erlang/== :record kind) (validate_struct_fields! (elem wanted 3)))
           (when-not (loaded_md5? mod expected)
            (when-not (and pair (erlang/== mod (elem pair 0))
                           (erlang/== expected (elem (elem (beam_lib/md5 (elem pair 1)) 1) 1)))
             (argument-error "canonical generated class artifact unavailable"))
            (BeamLisp.Env/publish_binaries! (list pair) "beam_lisp_class"))
           (when-not (loaded_md5? mod expected)
            (argument-error "generated class executable identity changed"))
           (register mod kind ns name (elem wanted 3))
           mod)))))))
(defn publish_declaration!
  "Source/compiler path. Validate one canonical descriptor, compile ONCE,
   then atomically fence publication plus immutable origin registration."
  [descriptor]
  (class_identity! descriptor)
  (let [pair (BeamLisp.Emit/compile_descriptor descriptor)
        expected (elem (elem (beam_lib/md5 (elem pair 1)) 1) 1)]
    (publish_class! descriptor pair expected)))
(defn replay_declaration!
  "Emitted/AOT path. Exact compiler-owned MD5, loaded artifact or ordinary
   object path; NO code generation or loaded-attribute trust. Same origin lock.
   AOT rewrites only actual canonical class producer calls to this form."
  [descriptor expected]
  (class_identity! descriptor)
  (let [mod (Map/fetch! descriptor :name)
        object (when-not (loaded_md5? mod expected) (code/get_object_code mod))
        pair (when (and (erlang/is_tuple object) (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size object))
                         (erlang/== mod (elem object 0))) (tuple mod (elem object 1)))]
    (publish_class! descriptor pair expected)))

(defn- create_module [mod kind fields]
  (let [beam (BeamLisp.Emit/compile_descriptor (class_descriptor mod kind fields))
        expected (elem (elem (beam_lib/md5 (elem beam 1)) 1) 1)]
    (BeamLisp.Env/with_module_locks (list mod)
      (fn []
        (when (and (erlang/not (loaded_md5? mod expected)) (BeamLisp.Env/live_code_leases? mod))
          (erlang/error (tuple :code_leased mod)))
        (BeamLisp.Env/publish_binaries! (list beam) "beam_lisp_record")))))

(defn- validate_struct_fields!
  [fields]
  (when (Enum/member? fields :__struct__)
    (argument-error "cannot set :__struct__ in struct definition"))
  (Enum/reduce fields (MapSet/new)
    (fn [field seen]
      (when (MapSet/member? seen field)
        (IO/warn (str "duplicate key " (Kernel/inspect field) " found in struct")))
      (MapSet/put seen field)))
  :ok)

(defn- struct_info_clauses
  "The `__info__/1` clauses Elixir's `defstruct` would generate, as
   `BeamLisp.Emit` clause data. Elixir's literal/pattern expander reads
   `__info__(:struct)`; `__struct__/0,1` alone supports runtime construction
   but not compilation against the type."
  [mod fields]
  (let [functions (list (tuple :__struct__ 0) (tuple :__struct__ 1))
        struct (Enum/map fields (fn [f] {:field f :default nil :required false}))
        values (list (tuple :module mod)
                     (tuple :functions functions)
                     (tuple :macros (list))
                     (tuple :deprecated (list))
                     (tuple :struct struct)
                     (tuple :exports_md5
                            (crypto/hash :md5 (erlang/term_to_binary (tuple functions struct)))))
        literals (Enum/map values
                   (fn [pair]
                     (BeamLisp.Emit/function_clause :__info__
                       (BeamLisp.Emit/lit (erlang/element 2 pair))
                       (list {:pop :plit :val (erlang/element 1 pair)}))))
        metadata (Enum/map (list :attributes :compile :md5)
                   (fn [key]
                     (BeamLisp.Emit/function_clause :__info__
                       (BeamLisp.Emit/remote :erlang :get_module_info
                         (list (BeamLisp.Emit/lit mod) (BeamLisp.Emit/lit key)))
                       (list {:pop :plit :val key}))))]
    (erlang/++ literals metadata)))
